# Environment variables — copy this file to .env.local and fill it in.
# Do NOT put real secrets in git. Do NOT commit .env.local (see .gitignore).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#   Purpose: Supabase project URL (REST + Auth + Storage endpoint).
#   Required: only for production (Supabase) mode. Leave blank to run in
#   local DEMO mode (data in data/works.json, see README).
#   Read by: lib/supabase/client.ts, lib/supabase/server.ts, and
#   lib/data/repository.ts (mode detection: set URL + anon key = Supabase
#   mode, otherwise demo mode). It is a public project identifier, but it
#   is still only read from the environment, never hard-coded.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   Purpose: Supabase anonymous (publishable) key. It is safe to ship to
#   the browser ONLY because Row Level Security + the public.admins
#   allowlist gate every write (see supabase/migrations/003).
#   Required: only for production (Supabase) mode; blank = demo mode.
#   Read by: lib/supabase/client.ts (browser login) and
#   lib/supabase/server.ts (server queries/actions, cookie session).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
#   Purpose: canonical production domain, e.g. https://your-domain.vercel.app.
#   Required: no — optional. If unset, lib/site.ts falls back to the
#   placeholder https://ai-lab.example, which is only correct for local
#   demo metadata/sitemap generation. Set the real domain before launch.
#   Read by: lib/site.ts siteUrl(), used in app/layout.tsx metadata,
#   app/works/[slug]/page.tsx canonical + Open Graph, app/sitemap.ts
#   and app/robots.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
#
# No service-role key is used anywhere in this project, on purpose.
# The server uses the ANON key + Row Level Security + the public.admins
# allowlist (see supabase/migrations/003). Do NOT add a service-role key
# here or in code: it would bypass RLS entirely if it ever leaked into
# a browser bundle or a log.
